+# Future-You Resume
+
+## Core idea
+
+Turn the resume from a backward-looking archive into a focused case file for the learner's next move. The visual story moves from cluttered history, through three common problems, to a clear evidence-building system and a final Resume Builder Tool handoff.
+
+## Visual approach
+
+- Use a crisp editorial workspace built from resume pages, evidence cards, scope markers, and a single gold through-line.
+- Keep each narration beat visually distinct while preserving a consistent navy, blue, gold, paper, and cultured-white system.
+- Make the transformation tangible: crowded task lists recede, impact evidence moves forward, and the Next Move Statement becomes the north star.
+- End with a clear, calm invitation to click Next and begin building.
+
+## Beat map
+
+1. Welcome and lesson title.
+2. The resume as an overloaded archive.
+3. Reframe it as a strategic tool.
+4. Introduce the three common culprits.
+5. Culprit one: tasks without impact.
+6. Culprit two: outdated language and format.
+7. Culprit three: no link to the next role.
+8. Show the decision-maker consequence.
+9. Flip to the future-you perspective.
+10. Curate evidence around one question.
+11. Build a case file from leadership, outcomes, and relevance.
+12. Make the Next Move Statement the north star.
+13. Select and rewrite three to five experiences.
+14. Transform a generic bullet into an impact statement.
+15. Hand off to the Resume Builder Tool.
+16. Close with the click-Next action.
+
