+# Design: Future-You Resume
+
+## Frame
+
+- 1920 × 1080, with at least 120px outer padding and a reserved lower footer zone.
+- Navy is the grounding color; paper-white resume surfaces supply contrast.
+- Blue identifies structure and direction. Gold identifies decisions, evidence, and forward motion.
+
+## Type
+
+- Proxima Nova (system fallback where unavailable).
+- Display: 96–112px, weight 900.
+- Headings: 60–72px, weight 900.
+- Body: 40–48px, weight 400 or 700.
+- Labels: 22–26px, uppercase, weight 700, tracked.
+
+## Composition language
+
+- A fixed lesson label and progress rail provide continuity.
+- Resume sheets use restrained borders, subtle shadows, and 12px corners.
+- Evidence chips and numbered markers turn abstract guidance into visible selections.
+- A gold line moves left-to-right as the narrative changes from history to next move.
+
+## Motion
+
+- One paused, seekable GSAP timeline drives every state.
+- Each beat enters in 0.4–0.6 seconds, settles by 1.2 seconds, and exits in 0.3 seconds.
+- Use short vertical reveals, line draws, card spreads, and emphasis pulses; never loop.
+- The final second adds a single gold arrow resolve toward the Next action.
+
+## Accessibility
+
+- Maintain high contrast on all text.
+- Keep meaningful body copy at 40px or larger.
+- Do not encode meaning with color alone; use labels, numbers, and position.
+- Keep animation finite and avoid rapid flashes.
+
